{"type":"record","name":"EsUnderlyingPrice","namespace":"com.optionsedge.contracts.hpsf","doc":"One es.underlying.es.price (es4) / underlying.es.price (prod) tick, published by options-edge-databento-feed. Until the 2026-11-02 cutover these topics carried hand-built JSON; each was wiped and recreated under its own name carrying Avro. The first twelve fields are UnderlyingPrice field for field and type for type (symbol ES, source NATIVE_ES_FUTURE, quality LIVE), so every reader of an underlying price tick decodes this record unchanged; the seven optional spxBasis* fields carry the ES->SPX basis mapping the feed stamps (absent when the feed has none). The registry subject is this record's FULL NAME (RecordNameStrategy), one subject for every environment whatever its TOPIC_PREFIX.","fields":[{"name":"schemaVersion","type":"int","doc":"Wire revision of the tick; 1 today."},{"name":"symbol","type":"string","doc":"ES. Also the Kafka record key."},{"name":"eventTime","type":"string","doc":"ISO-8601 UTC event time exactly as the feed stamped it (parsed with Instant.parse by every reader)."},{"name":"price","type":{"type":"bytes","logicalType":"decimal","precision":38,"scale":18},"doc":"The ES future price. The feed's double is written as the decimal of its shortest round-trip text, so BigDecimal.doubleValue() returns the identical double (exact, no rounding)."},{"name":"size","type":["null","long"],"doc":"Trade size; null (always null on this topic today).","default":null},{"name":"source","type":"string","doc":"Provenance token: NATIVE_ES_FUTURE."},{"name":"quality","type":"string","doc":"LIVE."},{"name":"canonicalSpot","type":{"type":"bytes","logicalType":"decimal","precision":38,"scale":18},"doc":"The canonical spot; equals price on this stream."},{"name":"spotEventTimeNs","type":"long","doc":"Canonical spot event clock, epoch nanoseconds."},{"name":"feedEpochId","type":"string","doc":"Feed epoch identity."},{"name":"epochSeq","type":"long","doc":"Monotonic sequence within the feed epoch."},{"name":"spotQuality","type":"string","doc":"Same token as quality."},{"name":"spxEquivalent","type":["null","double"],"doc":"ES price minus spxBasis, rounded half-even to 2 places; absent when no usable basis.","default":null},{"name":"spxBasis","type":["null","double"],"doc":"ES->SPX basis in index points, rounded half-even to 2 places; absent when UNAVAILABLE.","default":null},{"name":"spxBasisState","type":["null","string"],"doc":"MEASURED, ANCHORED, QUARANTINED, UNAVAILABLE ...; the basis engine's verdict. Absent when the feed stamped no basis.","default":null},{"name":"spxBasisMeasuredAtMs","type":["null","long"],"doc":"Epoch milliseconds of the basis reference measurement; absent when none.","default":null},{"name":"spxBasisAgeMs","type":["null","long"],"doc":"Age of the basis at publish, milliseconds, never negative.","default":null},{"name":"spxBasisUnavailableReason","type":["null","string"],"doc":"Why the basis is UNAVAILABLE (COLD_START, ...); present only with state UNAVAILABLE.","default":null},{"name":"spxBasisMadPts","type":["null","double"],"doc":"Median absolute deviation of the basis samples in points; present only for a MEASURED basis.","default":null}]}